// An `int` is neither a `float` nor a `decimal`, and this language does not convert one to the
// other behind your back -- so `math.floor(5)` is a compile error rather than a no-op returning 5.
//
// The message now lists all three declarations of `floor`, which it could not before `decimal`
// members joined the set: it used to name `float` alone, and a reader who actually had a decimal
// in hand learned nothing from it.
use math

fn main() {
    print(math.floor(5))
}
